.TH BABYSIT.CONF 5 "2026-11-15" "babysit" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
babysit.conf \- configuration for babysitd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/babysit/babysit.conf
.br
.I $HOME/.config/babysit/babysit.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
Settings for
.BR babysitd (8).
.BR babysit (1)
does not read this file.
Each line is
.IR key " = " value .
Blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
are ignored.
Unknown keys and bad values are reported and skipped.
.TP
.B max_age_days
Delete archived logs and finished logs older than this many days.
0 keeps them forever.
Default: 30.
.TP
.B compact_at_disk_percent
When the filesystem holding the logs is at least this full, in percent,
start a new log generation so that the logs written so far can be packed
and compressed.
0 disables.
Default: 90.
.TP
.B delete_at_disk_percent
When that filesystem is at least this full, in percent, delete packed logs
(archives of earlier boots and packed generations of the current boot),
oldest first, until it is not or none are left.
Live log directories are never deleted.
This is the only setting that removes logs before they reach
.BR max_age_days .
If the disk is full of other files it will delete every packed log without
bringing usage under the limit, so it is disabled unless set.
It is best set above
.BR compact_at_disk_percent ,
so that compression is tried first.
0 disables.
Default: 0.
.TP
.B check_interval
How often the service wakes up to do its housekeeping when nothing asks for
it sooner: a number with an
.BR s ,
.BR m ,
.B h
or
.B d
suffix (seconds if there is none).
.BR babysit (1)
wakes the service itself when it starts a new log generation, so this can
stay long.
Default: 6h.
.PP
Command-line options of
.B babysitd
override this file.
The file is read once, when the service starts.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
max_age_days = 14
compact_at_disk_percent = 80
delete_at_disk_percent = 95
check_interval = 12h
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR babysitd (8),
.BR babysit (1)
